    "body": "Here is a more slimed down 1 file version:\n```html\n<?php\n// Enabling these headers will result in the worker being restarted for every page navigation!\n// header(\"Cache-Control: no-store, no-cache, must-revalidate\");\n?>\n<!DOCTYPE html><html><head></head><body><a>Second Page</a><script>\n    const url = `data:application/javascript,const%20t%3DDate.now()%3BaddEventListener('connect'%2Ce%3D%3Ee.ports%5B0%5D.postMessage(t))`\n    globalThis.worker = new SharedWorker(url, \"test\")\n    worker.port.onmessage = function(event) {\n        const a = document.querySelector(\"a\")\n        const t = +new URL(location).searchParams.get(\"time\")\n        a.href = `?time=${event.data}&_=${Math.random()}`\n        if (!t) return\n        a.innerText = t === event.data ?\n            \"Worker installation time is the same ✅\" :\n            \"Worker installation time changed ❌\"\n    }\n    worker.port.start()\n</script></body></html>\n```\n\nSeems like in chrome, doing a refresh will reinstall the SharedWorker (unlike FF & Safari)",
