    "updated_at": "2025-05-10T16:35:34Z",
    "body": "I can confirm with Chrome 136.0.7103.93 (Official Build) (arm64) on macOS 15.4.1 (24E263) – test reports `Worker installation time changed ❌` after enabling the Cache-Control header.\n\nBut for me so does Firefox 138.0.1 (aarch64) (also macOS 15.4.1 24E263) – at least after the 3rd or 4th click I also see the  `Worker installation time changed ❌` \n\nMy initial test still behaves as described with current versions of Chrome and Firefox.\n\nOnly Safari (18.4 (20621.1.15.11.10))  consistently reports `Worker installation time is the same ✅]` even with Cache-Control header turned on. I cannot use my test in Safari, as I do not know how to see the Shared Worker's console in Safari...\n\n\nI guess issuing a bug report to Chrome/Chromium and Firefox/Gecko team would be the next step.\n\nNever did that before - is this the way to go: ?\nhttps://issues.chromium.org/issues \nhttps://bugzilla.mozilla.org/\n",
